&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week4-2026-10-26"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 4: Ghost in the Machine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  🕯️ What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  The Thin Veil Between Past and Present
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;October 31 marks the arrival of &lt;strong&gt;Halloween&lt;/strong&gt;, which flows seamlessly into &lt;strong&gt;Día de los Muertos&lt;/strong&gt; on November 1 and 2—a sacred stretch on the calendar when ancient folklore tells us the barrier between the living world and the spirit realm grows thin.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In Mexican tradition, no one is truly gone as long as their story is remembered (&lt;em&gt;"No hay muerte verdadera mientras haya memoria"&lt;/em&gt;). Every autumn, families build &lt;em&gt;ofrendas&lt;/em&gt;—tiered altars glowing with candlelight, fragrant copal incense, and golden marigold petals (&lt;em&gt;cempasúchil&lt;/em&gt;)—to welcome the souls of ancestors back for one night of feasting, music, and love.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At the exact same time, inside our modern computers, a parallel haunting takes place: the foundational algorithms, compiler paradigms, and mathematical discoveries of computing legends—&lt;strong&gt;Ada Lovelace&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Alan Turing&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Grace Hopper&lt;/strong&gt;, and even ancient languages like &lt;strong&gt;COBOL&lt;/strong&gt;—continue to execute in our silicon every millisecond. They are the literal &lt;strong&gt;"Ghost in the Machine"&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Introducing Ofrenda Viva AI
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://ath1614.github.io/OfrendaViva-AI/" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Ofrenda Viva AI&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is an on-device, 100% local Día de los Muertos remembrance sanctuary and haunted terminal séance powered by &lt;strong&gt;Google Gemma 2 (2B)&lt;/strong&gt; and styled with &lt;strong&gt;React Bits by DavidHDev&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It offers two interconnected realities:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;🌼 The Sacred Día de los Muertos Altar (Three Tiers of Memory)&lt;/strong&gt;:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 1 (El Cielo / The Heavens)&lt;/strong&gt;: Copal incense smoke, pure virgin beeswax candles, and celestial guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 2 (La Tierra / Earth &amp;amp; Ancestors)&lt;/strong&gt;: Framed portraits of departed loved ones, family elders, and computing pioneers. Clicking any portrait reveals their life story, authentic Mexican &lt;em&gt;Calaverita Literaria&lt;/em&gt; poem, and consecrated offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tier 3 (El Inframundo / The Offerings)&lt;/strong&gt;: Traditional &lt;em&gt;Pan de Muerto&lt;/em&gt; dusted with orange blossom sugar, clay cups of frothed Mexican chocolate (&lt;em&gt;champurrado&lt;/em&gt;), sugar skulls (&lt;em&gt;calaveras&lt;/em&gt;), purifying salt, and water to quench weary souls after the long journey from Mictlán.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;👻 Ghost in the Machine Mode (Retro CRT Terminal Séance)&lt;/strong&gt;:

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A single click transmutes the golden candlelit sanctuary into an eerie 1980s green phosphor CRT monitor with scanlines, cathode hum, and chromatic aberration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive Offline Séance&lt;/strong&gt;: Hold real-time terminal dialogues with the ghosts of computing pioneers (Ada Lovelace, Alan Turing, Grace Hopper, The Ghost of COBOL, or your own custom family ancestors) decrypted live through the screen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




