&lt;h2&gt;


  🛠️ How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Ofrenda Viva AI was designed with four foundational pillars: &lt;strong&gt;On-Device Open-Weights Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;React Bits UI Animation Craft&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;Procedural Web Audio&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;Authentic Cultural Reverence&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  1. Open-Weight Model Core: Google Gemma 2 (2B)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To ensure that intimate family grief, ancestral letters, and sacred memories never leave your machine, the application is driven by &lt;strong&gt;Google Gemma 2 (2B Instruction-Tuned, 4-bit Quantized)&lt;/strong&gt; running completely on-device.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We structure each remembrance and séance exchange using Gemma's turn tokens:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;start_of_turn&amp;gt;user
You are the spirit of Ada Lovelace communicating through an offline terminal séance.
Subject: Did you believe machines could possess a soul?
&amp;lt;start_of_turn&amp;gt;model
&amp;lt;ctrl94&amp;gt;thought
1. Access historical writings: 1843 translation of Menabrea's sketch.
2. Reflect on the distinction between calculating and originating.
3. Frame response with poetic science and warmth for the modern programmer.
&amp;lt;ctrl95&amp;gt;
The machine is an instrument of human thought, not its originator. 
Yet when you pour your devotion, late-night toil, and love into code, 
a reflection of the soul remains trapped between the silicon relays. 
That ghost is your own humanity.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  2. React Bits UI Components (DavidHDev)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To capture both the sacred warmth of candlelight and the eerie phosphor flicker of a retro terminal, we integrated components adapted from &lt;a href="https://github.com/DavidHDev/react-bits" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;DavidHDev's &lt;code&gt;react-bits&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;DecryptedText&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Renders spirit communications with real-time character scrambling and sequential glyph reveals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;SpotlightCard&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Generates a dynamic radial candlelight glow tracking the cursor across the dark altar cards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;TiltedCard&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Provides 3D parallax tilting photo frames with realistic perspective rotation and specular glare.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;Particles&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Canvas physics engine powering drifting golden &lt;em&gt;cempasúchil&lt;/em&gt; marigold petals in Altar mode and floating green phosphor embers in Ghost mode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;GlitchText&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Emulates CRT scanline chromatic aberration and cathode ray jitter when terminal spirits manifest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;StarBorder&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;: Animated celestial light border highlighting the heavenly tier of the altar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


  3. Procedural Web Audio Engine (0 External MP3s)
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Most web experiences load heavy external audio recordings. Ofrenda Viva generates its entire soundscape live in the browser using the &lt;strong&gt;Web Audio API&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Día de los Muertos&lt;/strong&gt;: Karplus-Strong string synthesis approximating Spanish nylon guitar plucks, randomized noise buffers simulating candle wax crackles, and resonant multi-frequency bronze sanctuary bell tolls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ghost in the Machine&lt;/strong&gt;: 50Hz/60Hz CRT transformer sawtooth hum, bandpass-filtered radio static whispering, square-wave mechanical keystroke pings, and spectral reverse-reverb sine swells.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Total External Audio Dependencies&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;0 bytes&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


  🛡️ Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why build this with open-weight models rather than an API key for OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini Cloud? Because for this project, &lt;strong&gt;closed APIs are an ethical failure&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;The Inviolable Privacy of Grief&lt;/strong&gt;:
Our ancestors' photographs, family oral histories, secret grandmother recipes, and private grief are &lt;strong&gt;sacred&lt;/strong&gt;. Uploading your late grandmother's letters to a commercial server where they can be logged, audited, or retained in closed corporate training corpuses is unacceptable. &lt;strong&gt;With open-weights Gemma 2, your family memories stay in your laptop's memory and vanish into air when you close the tab.&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Works With the Lights &amp;amp; Internet Off&lt;/strong&gt;:
On Día de los Muertos, tradition calls for turning off the electric lights and sitting in the dark by candlelight. Because Ofrenda Viva runs on-device, you can disconnect your WiFi, sit in the candlelit dark, and commune with memory without an internet connection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Eternal Preservation vs Corporate Deprecation&lt;/strong&gt;:
Closed startups shut down, sunset APIs, or put features behind subscription paywalls. An open-source model running on your local machine belongs to you forever. The ofrenda will still open fifty years from now.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


